    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταληκτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leaving off</i>; esp. in Metric, of verses <i>having
				the last foot incomplete</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				4.2
			</span></i>, Anon.Metr.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				220ix 19
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
			</span></i> l.c.; of feet, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ</span>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶδος παίωνος</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>disinterestedly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διδόναι τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					9.42
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.13
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ληπτ-</span> codd.), <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.23.46
			</span></i>.</div>
